{"document_id":"cir-beta-glucan-safety-assessment-v1","title":"Beta-Glucan — CIR safety-assessment factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/1091581816651606","published_year":2016,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased CIR conclusion: in the Safety Assessment of Microbial Polysaccharide Gums (2016) the CIR Expert Panel concluded the assessed gums, including Beta-Glucan, are safe in the present practices of use and concentration in cosmetics. Beta-glucan was reported as practically non-irritating to rabbit eyes (weakly irritating in a HET-CAM assay). Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim CIR text is stored.","source_locator":"Safety Assessment of Microbial Polysaccharide Gums as Used in Cosmetics (CIR, 2016).","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review. Safety Assessment of Microbial Polysaccharide Gums as Used in Cosmetics. Int J Toxicol. 2016.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["beta-glucan"],"ingredient_names":["Beta-Glucan"],"inci_names":["Beta-Glucan"],"card_role":"grounding_evidence_only","selection_authority":"ingredient_governance_record","selection_authority_note":"routine_selection_allowed=false on this evidence card means the card itself can never authorise a routine. Whether an ingredient may be selected is decided by its governed ingredient record